# Next.js UI (Renderer)

## Framework — Next.js App Router

- Use **App Router** under `src/app/` — not Pages Router.
- Prefer **Client Components** (`'use client'`) for interactive UI (chat, settings, theme toggle).
- Use **Server Components** only when they add value; Electron loads static export, so most UI is client-side.
- Do not add Next.js API routes for AW/LLM — use Electron IPC via `window.jerry`.

## Component library — shadcn/ui (strict)

All UI is built with [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs). Components live in `src/components/ui/`.

- **Install on need only**: `npx shadcn@latest add <component>` when a feature requires it.
- **No raw HTML controls** for interactive UI — use shadcn primitives:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button onClick={send}>Send</button>
<input value={text} onChange={...} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input'
<Button onClick={send}>Send</Button>
<Input value={text} onChange={...} />
```

- Do not add custom CSS or Tailwind overrides unless the user explicitly asks for extra styling.
- Compose features from shadcn components; modify source in `src/components/ui/` only when shadcn defaults are insufficient.

## Theme

- **Default**: dark
- **Options**: `dark` | `light` | `system`
- **Base color**: gray
- Use `next-themes` with `ThemeProvider` in `src/app/layout.tsx`; persist preference via electron-store in main when wired up.

## Icons — Lucide React

- Use `lucide-react` exclusively — no other icon libraries.
- Import named icons: `import { Send, Settings } from 'lucide-react'`

## Structure

```
src/
  app/              # Next.js routes (layout.tsx, page.tsx)
  components/
    ui/             # shadcn components (CLI-managed)
    Chat/           # feature components
  lib/utils.ts      # cn() helper
  store/            # Zustand stores
```

## Accessibility

- shadcn/Radix handle most a11y; prefer shadcn Dialog, Label, etc. over hand-rolled markup.
- Chat messages: `role="log"` with `aria-live="polite"` for Jerry replies.

## Electron renderer constraints

- Call main-process features via `window.jerry` (preload), not `require` or direct localhost fetch for AW/LLM unless routed through main.
